_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"GoGss2SqsUPwP0xcI9IUuw","review_id":"GJ48cD4jKoqVpj3dubI8sQ","date":"2016-01-15T16:24:28","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9401769042015076,"text_excerpt":"There are only a few decent coffee shops in the French Quarter, and Spitfire Espresso Bar is top notch. You won't find a vast menu of fancy drinks. Instead, you'll see a small selection of four or five regional coffees served via pour over (Hario V60), as well as one or two iced cofee options. There are also a few espresso drinks, such as cappuccino, lattes, etc. The proprietor was very friendly and knowledgeable (his name escapes me). He answered my questions about the available coffees. The shop is very small, with seating for maybe 4 people max. But if you just want to grab a great cup of coffee on the go, this is your place. Highly recommend it!"},{"business_id":"GoGss2SqsUPwP0xcI9IUuw","review_id":"SJCnviBYraSr-OF_29xxgg","date":"2016-02-10T21:34:32","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9334350824356079,"text_excerpt":"This place is about the size of a closet, but let me tell you, they might have the best coffee in New Orleans. I was so happy to find out that they had Panther Coffee beans here (from Miami), they have my favorite espresso blend right now. I would have taken this espresso intravenously if I could. Baristas here are properly trained and super friendly. They are also doing really cool stuff with bitters in their coffee which I have not tried. That being said, I haven't been to every coffee shop in town but this is the best IMO."},{"business_id":"GoGss2SqsUPwP0xcI9IUuw","review_id":"4F-TbBDxyu1-CEzHnsLm5A","date":"2018-09-27T06:56:53","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9308477640151978,"text_excerpt":"Made a quick stop here for some real coffee after a short walk from Cafe Du Monde. Spitfire Espresso is conveniently located near Jackson Square, and it's a inconspicuous little shop that can surely go unnoticed if you're not looking out for it. That would be terrible, as this coffee shop is probably the best option in the French Quarter for true specialty coffee - all else there is either drinking related, food, or souvenir shops and boutiques. Well as mentioned, the place is small, closet room small almost (exaggerating, don't fret). So any thoughts of having coffee and hanging out might just go out the window, unless you're able to snag one of the stools placed by the petite wall count..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"GoGss2SqsUPwP0xcI9IUuw","photo_id":"W9e7iRxH0J2RhJtctN0QwQ","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/W9e7iRxH0J2RhJtctN0QwQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8817492127418518},{"business_id":"GoGss2SqsUPwP0xcI9IUuw","photo_id":"GplBF5D4yV174v3SIM81Cg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/GplBF5D4yV174v3SIM81Cg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8527228832244873},{"business_id":"GoGss2SqsUPwP0xcI9IUuw","photo_id":"gDnCkzFz8fl4LUWWTyn7IA","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/gDnCkzFz8fl4LUWWTyn7IA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8263071775436401},{"business_id":"GoGss2SqsUPwP0xcI9IUuw","photo_id":"3AIvoWso8y60p3cle8dB9w","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/3AIvoWso8y60p3cle8dB9w.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7953100204467773},{"business_id":"GoGss2SqsUPwP0xcI9IUuw","photo_id":"uzlZZfQpOuukzwKOOKM0DQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/uzlZZfQpOuukzwKOOKM0DQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7600007653236389}]},"notebook_case":null}
